// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_SECRET_EXFILTRATION
// Phase 2 slice 1 — `docs/CLAIMS.md` item 21, "unannotated return place types".
//
// RUNTIME-PROVEN false accept before this fixture existed: `check` exited 0 and `run` PRINTED 42.
//
// Mechanism: a function with no `-> T` records the EMPTY STRING in `fn_ret_types`, and
// `place_struct_type`'s `Expr::Call` arm filters empty spellings before consulting the struct
// field table. The declared `secret<i64>` on `Box.k` therefore vanished for every field read off
// a factory result. The fix infers the nominal return type from the body, and ONLY when every
// return site constructs the same type, so the resolver can never attribute one struct's
// qualifiers to another value.
struct Box { k: secret<i64> }

fn make() {
    return Box { k: 42 };
}

fn main() {
    print(make().k);
}
